1
00:00:03,068 --> 00:00:03,290
Shh…

2
00:00:03,340 --> 00:00:03,766
A cave!

3
00:00:03,816 --> 00:00:05,805
Huge halls under the mountain,

4
00:00:05,855 --> 00:00:08,387
stone spikes hanging from the ceiling.

5
00:00:08,437 --> 00:00:09,797
Who carved all this?

6
00:00:10,635 --> 00:00:10,939
Drip.

7
00:00:10,989 --> 00:00:11,292
Drip.

8
00:00:11,342 --> 00:00:13,201
One drop every ten seconds.

9
00:00:13,251 --> 00:00:14,050
Noah laughs:

10
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:17,443
a drop of water isn't going to carve a mountain!

11
00:00:17,493 --> 00:00:18,059
And yet…

12
00:00:18,822 --> 00:00:20,336
Discovery mission!

13
00:00:22,852 --> 00:00:23,416
Mini mode!

14
00:00:23,466 --> 00:00:25,689
Passing through the air and the soil,

15
00:00:25,739 --> 00:00:27,779
rainwater picks up carbon dioxide.

16
00:00:27,829 --> 00:00:29,868
It becomes just a tiny bit acidic,

17
00:00:29,918 --> 00:00:31,331
like a sugar-free soda.

18
00:00:32,112 --> 00:00:35,001
This water slips into cracks in the limestone,

19
00:00:35,051 --> 00:00:37,046
a rock it knows how to dissolve.

20
00:00:37,096 --> 00:00:39,218
Drop after drop, the crack widens:

21
00:00:39,268 --> 00:00:40,802
a corridor, then a hall.

22
00:00:41,570 --> 00:00:42,492
And the stone spikes?

23
00:00:42,542 --> 00:00:46,938
The water reaches the cave loaded with limestone, loses its gas, and the limestone settles back:

24
00:00:46,988 --> 00:00:50,275
a stalactite grows from the ceiling, a stalagmite rises from the floor.

25
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:52,764
Look: chalk is limestone.

26
00:00:52,814 --> 00:00:56,009
In vinegar, an acid, it melts away in bubbles!

27
00:00:56,059 --> 00:00:59,022
Rainwater does the same, much more slowly.

28
00:00:59,792 --> 00:01:01,808
That's how caves are carved out.

29
00:01:03,322 --> 00:01:07,250
Rainwater, slightly acidic, dissolves limestone drop by drop:

30
00:01:07,300 --> 00:01:09,387
millions of years later, a cave.

31
00:01:10,198 --> 00:01:11,008
With an adult:

32
00:01:11,058 --> 00:01:13,649
put a piece of chalk in a glass of vinegar.

33
00:01:13,699 --> 00:01:14,141
Bubbles!

34
00:01:14,191 --> 00:01:15,554
Come back the next day:

35
00:01:15,604 --> 00:01:17,201
the chalk has melted away.

36
00:01:17,982 --> 00:01:19,140
And why does the sky

37
00:01:19,190 --> 00:01:20,953
light up green near the poles?

38
00:01:21,003 --> 00:01:22,211
The answer tomorrow.
